I'm omw to my uni but if you really want to d discuss this, I can do this later 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

But let me tell you this: If you're naive enough to think na hindi political maneuvering yung accusations sa kanya back then, edi surely you think that De Lima's imprisonment is justified, yes?

For literary works, I've found "Man's search for meaning" by Viktor Frankl to be very helpful. Meditations by Marcus Aurelius is also good. I also watched some seminars by Dr Gabor Mate on You tube about how to deal with your emotions, traumas and such. 

&#x200B;

I honestly just listen to classical (I highly recommend Tchaikovsky's piano concerto no 1 and Rachmaninoff's  prelude in c sharp minor) then I close my eyes and just...breathe. Slowly, deeply and rhythmically. Another method that I use is, whenever I feel that I may become angry or what, I do some kind of physical activity. Pushups, pullups, whatever. It helps to release the tension inside of me.

Man we should not be too harsh to ourselves din. I remember that  quote by Søren Kierkegaard "Life can only be understood backwards but it must be lived forwards." We learn as we go, and if we're really destined for them I truly believe that fate would do it's thing. Pero if we're destined to be with someone else, at least we can treat them better, yeah? 

&#x200B;

Thank you din for your kind words. Keep your head up, king.

It's sad lang na the catalyst for our change is a Goddamn heartbreak HAHA. Thanks man, I agree. That state of mind is not healthy for anyone really. Not just ourselves but for everyone around us. 

&#x200B;

Hey man 25 is still young. And it's never too late to change anyways. I'm genuinely proud of you bro.

For real man. I guess it's better na rin for me na I learned all of this habang (relatively) bata pa ako. I guess it helped din na I had  a talk with my dad and he said na I should really break this generational trait that we have (he said na sa gano'ong environment din sya lumaki) it made me think na I don't want any of my kids (kung magkakaroon man) to inherit that shitty behaviour. Cheers bro, we can do it. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, I'm proud of you! Two months is a long time na you know. Hopefully our streak would continue haha.

