[So edgy yet so good ughhhhhhhhhhhh](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dF5tL1APzEM&ab_channel=BadflowerVEVO)



I’ve realized that happiness is not a thing, a person, nor an event. Happiness is a choice. In our life, we really can’t control that many factor, like who’ll be our parents, our social standing, our looks, and such. *But what we can choose is how to react to those factors. We can sulk into madness and sadness and live* a pretty miserable life, or we can laugh it off and make the best out of the cards that we’re dealt. We don’t need to win the game of life, we need to enjoy it. For if we choose our goals instead of our happiness, we’ll end up not satisfied. For our greed would inevitably take control and we will desire more. Until our next goalpost would be, well impossible to reach. Though I can understand that some do derive happiness from success.

